## Carry forward

1. Retain20k. Five wins, nineteen losses and two draws at this rank; do not infer consistent strength from one large win.
2. Broaden viable bases before contact forces repeated replies. This C3/G7/C5/G5/C7 continuation retained both side regions; game28's unsupported upper strip did not.
3. Count early with explicit coordinates and distinguish internal eye moves, retained endpoints and genuine expansion. Here44 lost J4/J5 to42, gained D1/D2/D3 to45, then F8/F7/F5/G4 to49.
4. Repair actual connections promptly: G6, H5, H6, C6 and C4. Inspect all orthogonal same-color neighbors; Black E2 joined E3/F2 and J3 joined both right branches.
5. Secure first-line boundaries before the undercut: D1/C9/G9 retained selected room. Opponent replies made these successful; no alternate move is established as inferior.
6. Divide eye room deliberately: H8/J8 created two true two-point spaces; B5/A5 separated two large left eye regions.
7. Finish neutral boundaries under Chinese scoring after life. Four added right points enlarged the win; filling internal territory to establish eyes preserved rather than increased area.
8. This win had no captures, no lost stones and no ignored-atari rescue. Territorial development and life can produce sufficient area without chasing a central capture.
